B) Using Z-distribution
Used when:

Sample size is large
Population standard deviation is known
Consider the following example. A random sample of 50 adult females was taken and their RBC count is measured. The sample mean is 4.63 and the standard deviation of
RBC count is 0.54. Construct a 95% confidence interval estimate for the true mean RBC count in adult females.

from scipy import stats
import numpy as np

mean = 4.63
std_dev = 0.54
n = 50
z = 1.960

se = std_dev / np.sqrt(n)
moe = z * se

lower = mean - moe
upper = mean + moe

print(f"Confidence Interval: ({lower:.3f}, {upper:.3f})")

OUPUT 
----Confidence Interval: (4.480, 4.780)
